com/bb_api.h: add BB_EVENT_UNKNOWN_12/BB_EVENT_RETX_TOO_MANY, widen BB_EVENT_MAX

The AR8030 baseband pushes a retx-pressure event to the host that the
vendor streamer binary (ar_ldyhs_sky) subscribes to and uses to trigger
a bitrate cut (fpv_video_buffer_cache_monitor() polls
fpv_bb_is_send_retx_too_many(), which returns true off this event, and
calls fpv_video_set_venc_bitrate()) -- but the event's own id, 13, is
one past bb_event_e's own BB_EVENT_MAX (12) and is not enumerated in
this SDK build's own header at all. A neighboring id, 12, is
independently confirmed to exist too (also subscribed by fpv_bb_init,
its own callback posts a different local event, purpose not traced).

Recovered by tracing backwards from fpv_bb_is_send_retx_too_many()
(Ghidra decompile of ar_ldyhs_sky) rather than forwards from a log
string, since this function itself calls no ioctl at all -- it only
reads two process-local flags. The flag setter is caseD_64's own
`case 0x16` in a local event-FIFO dispatch loop (com_event_fifo_read/
write, an internal IPC detail of the vendor binary, not part of this
SDK), which is itself reached only via a callback registered against
BB_EVENT id 13 in fpv_bb_init's own BB_SET_EVENT_SUBSCRIBE calls --
confirmed by resolving that callback's own relocation-encoded address
(0x67b7c) and disassembling it: it loads r1=0x16 (the local event type
caseD_64 branches on) before the call that posts it. The neighboring
callback for id 12 was independently found to post a different local
event type (0x13), cross-confirming the address resolution method
rather than resting on a single data point.

Added as real bb_event_e enumerators, not a same-value #define past
the enum (an earlier draft of this patch tried that, to avoid touching
BB_EVENT_MAX's own value) -- because BB_EVENT_MAX has to actually widen
for either id to work at all: confirmed live on real hardware that the
already-deployed ar8030d binary hard-rejects any event id >=
BB_EVENT_MAX at the RPC layer before the request ever reaches the
firmware (daemon/callback_node.c's rpc_cb_read(): `if ((pack.reqid &
0xffff) >= BB_EVENT_MAX) { pack.sta = -2; ... }`) -- confirmed via the
daemon's own per-connection debug log showing this exact code path
firing for a live subscribe attempt on id 13. No fixed-size array
anywhere in this SDK/daemon tree is sized by BB_EVENT_MAX (checked
across the whole tree), so widening it from 12 to 14 is safe.

This means the fix requires rebuilding ar8030d itself against this
header, not just the client library -- BB_SET_EVENT_SUBSCRIBE's own
client-side plumbing (app/ar8030/session_callback.c) has no bounds
check of its own and already forwards any event id to the daemon
unconditionally; it's the daemon's own compiled-in BB_EVENT_MAX that
gates acceptance.

See ar8030-transport's own commit adding this event's subscription to
tx/bitrate_ctl.c for how it's actually used -- treated as a
conservative "react to the firing, don't parse `arg`" signal, since
the event's own payload layout beyond what the vendor app's own local
re-derivation shows is not independently confirmed.

Mirrors sbc-groundstations' own identical patch.

diff --git a/com/bb_api.h b/com/bb_api.h
--- a/com/bb_api.h
+++ b/com/bb_api.h
@@ -501,6 +501,56 @@
     BB_EVENT_MCS_CHANGE_END,                                    /**<@note MCS等级发生变化结束事件*/
     BB_EVENT_PRJ_DISPATCH2_UART,                                /**<@note 项目自定义事件分发2(用于UART RPC)*/
     BB_EVENT_PRJ_DISPATCH2_SDIO,                                /**<@note 项目自定义事件分发2(用于SDIO RPC)*/
+    /**<@note id 12 -- NOT enumerated by this SDK build at all before this
+     * fix. Independently confirmed via Ghidra decompile (ar_ldyhs_sky's
+     * own fpv_bb_init subscribes it) to exist and to be distinct from id
+     * 13 below (its own callback posts a different local event, type
+     * 0x13, to this app's own internal com_event_fifo -- purpose not
+     * further traced). Named generically since its actual meaning is
+     * unconfirmed; do not assume it means anything more specific than
+     * "the vendor app also subscribes to this". */
+    BB_EVENT_UNKNOWN_12,
+    /**<@note Fires when the baseband's own retx pressure crosses a
+     * threshold internal to the firmware. Independently confirmed by
+     * this project via Ghidra decompile, tracing all the way from the
+     * vendor streamer's own fpv_bb_is_send_retx_too_many() (the function
+     * fpv_video_buffer_cache_monitor() polls to decide whether to cut
+     * fpv_video_set_venc_bitrate()) back to its actual trigger:
+     * fpv_bb_init subscribes id 13 via BB_SET_EVENT_SUBSCRIBE with a
+     * callback that, on firing, posts a local event (type 0x16, via
+     * this app's own internal com_event_fifo_write -- a local IPC
+     * detail of the vendor binary, not part of this SDK) which in turn
+     * sets the one-shot flag fpv_bb_is_send_retx_too_many() reads. That
+     * confirms fpv_bb_is_send_retx_too_many() itself calls no ioctl at
+     * all -- it is purely driven by this event, not by
+     * BB_GET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS (that opcode's own struct carries no
+     * usable telemetry at all, see its own doc comment -- an unrelated
+     * dead end independently discovered by this project). arg's layout
+     * for this event is NOT independently confirmed (the vendor app's
+     * own re-derived local payload, after passing through its own
+     * com_event_fifo indirection, has a gating byte at offset 6 --
+     * `payload[6] == 1` -- with a separate value at offset 5 always
+     * latched elsewhere regardless; whether bb_event_callback's own
+     * `arg` for this event matches that same layout directly, or needs
+     * different offsets, is unverified). Treat any firing as a
+     * conservative "radio is actively under repair pressure" hint
+     * rather than parsing `arg` -- see ar8030-transport's own
+     * tx/bitrate_ctl.c for how this is used (react to the firing
+     * itself, own rate limit, do not dereference `arg`).
+     *
+     * Both id 12 and this one were confirmed, on real hardware, to be
+     * rejected outright by the currently-deployed ar8030d binary: its
+     * own daemon/callback_node.c hard-rejects any event id >=
+     * BB_EVENT_MAX at the RPC layer (`pack.sta = -2`) before the
+     * request ever reaches the firmware. BB_EVENT_MAX did not cover
+     * either id until this fix added them as real enum entries (rather
+     * than a same-value #define past the enum, which this fix replaces)
+     * so that BB_EVENT_MAX itself widens to 14 and the daemon's own
+     * check, compiled against this header, passes both ids once
+     * ar8030d itself is rebuilt against it -- confirmed no fixed-size
+     * array anywhere in this SDK/daemon tree is sized by BB_EVENT_MAX,
+     * so widening it is safe. */
+    BB_EVENT_RETX_TOO_MANY,
     BB_EVENT_MAX
 } bb_event_e;
 
